          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Node-to-node network tests\n\nOne `network-mesh-probe` pod runs on every node with pod networking, so the tests traverse the Calico pod network and its pod-CIDR routes. Every 60 seconds each probe sends 10 ICMP echo requests to every other probe pod:\n\n- **Ping** - 10 ICMP echo requests, 200 ms apart. The table shows the selected aggregation of RTT and packet loss over the range.\n- **Upload** - every 30 minutes, runs a 3-second iperf3 TCP test with 16 parallel streams to the peer and records the receiver-side throughput.\n- **Download** - runs the same iperf3 test in reverse (`-R`) and records the receiver-side throughput.\n\nRows are the node running the test (`source`), columns are the peer (`destination`). The **Aggregation** variable at the top selects how each table reduces the samples over the dashboard time range: `max`, `min`, `avg`, `p50`, `p95`, `p99` or `latest`. Upload tests send data from row to column; download tests send data from column to row. The tests are phase-shifted across nodes, so the full mesh is not saturated at once.\n\nMetrics are scraped from each probe pod's IP on port 9101 by the `network-mesh-probe` PodMonitor. Long-term history is available through the Thanos data source.\n"
      },
      "title": "How this works",
      "type": "text"
    },
